@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title Base image layers — builder stages, the jlink runtime, and what must share a RUN

' purpose: how proveo/base, base-node and base-node-lsp are actually assembled —
'          stage ordering, pinning by digest, and the same-RUN rule that makes a
'          deletion save bytes rather than only hide a path
' covers: defs/base/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/base/build.sh
' covers: defs/base/ensure.sh
' covers: defs/base-node/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/base-node/build.sh
' covers: defs/base-node-lsp/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/base-node-lsp/build.sh
'
' Lineage rules (which parent, which tag, ensure.sh's two modes) are
' _spec/_devops/image-lineage-and-publish.puml. The size ARGUMENT and the
' fleet-wide measurements are _spec/_plans/image-size-reduction.puml. This file
' is the current-state record of how the three shared layers are built.
'
' ── STAGE 1: ONE proveo-entrypoint BUILDER FOR THE WHOLE FLEET ──────────────
' `FROM golang:1.26-trixie AS proveo-entrypoint-builder`. Built once, in
' defs/base, and every harness inherits the binary instead of recompiling it in
' its own stage.
'
' The stage's internal order is deliberate and was arrived at by watching builds
' re-run:
'
'   COPY go.mod go.sum ./ ; RUN go mod download
'       module downloads cached separately from source.
'   RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 GOBIN=/out go install github.com/ptdewey/plantuml-lsp@latest
'       ABOVE the source copy on purpose: plantuml-lsp is fetched from upstream
'       and owes nothing to this repo's source. Below the copy, every edit in the
'       tree re-ran the install.
'   COPY cmd ./cmd ; COPY internal ./internal
'       `COPY cmd` + `COPY internal`, NEVER `COPY . .` — the same shape
'       defs/sidecars/egress-proxy/Dockerfile already used.
'   RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath -ldflags='-s -w' -o /out/proveo-entrypoint ./cmd/proveo-entrypoint
'
' WHY THE NARROW COPY. The build context is the REPO ROOT (every def builds from
' there), which carries 201 MB of node_modules and 83 MB of apps/. `COPY . .`
' baked all of it into this layer AND invalidated the build below on any file in
' the tree — a README edit re-ran the compile. `./cmd/proveo-entrypoint` needs
' internal/entrypoint and internal/verify and nothing else: the root package's
' embeds are not in its dependency graph, so defs/ and packages/ are not required
' here. The root .dockerignore stops the rest from reaching the daemon at all.
'
' ── STAGE 2: THE JRE, BUILT WITH jlink, NOT INSTALLED ───────────────────────
' `default-jre-headless` was the largest single package in this image — dpkg
' Installed-Size 198,806 kB — and its only consumer is /opt/plantuml.jar. Because
' it sits in proveo/base it was paid by every harness, every browser variant and
' every sidecar descendant: all 14 published images.
'
' `FROM debian:trixie-slim AS jre-builder` installs `openjdk-21-jdk-headless`
' AND `binutils`, then runs jlink. binutils is not optional: `jlink
' --strip-debug` shells out to `objcopy` on Debian's OpenJDK and fails with
' "Cannot run program objcopy" without it. It joins the BUILDER stage only, which
' ships nothing into the final image.
'
' MEASURED on this JDK: 72 MB against 194 MB, rendering -tpng and -tsvg
' identically (verified before it landed).
'
' THE MODULE LIST IS NOT THE MINIMUM, and that is the decision:
'   java.base, java.compiler, java.desktop, java.instrument, java.logging,
'   java.management, java.naming, java.net.http, java.prefs, java.rmi,
'   java.scripting, java.sql, java.xml, jdk.attach, jdk.compiler, jdk.crypto.ec,
'   jdk.jartool, jdk.jdi, jdk.unsupported, jdk.zipfs
'   --strip-debug --no-header-files --no-man-pages --compress=zip-6
' A plantuml-only prune is 59 MB and would break jdtls: `_install_jdtls`
' provisions its own Java 21 only when `_java_major` reports < 21, and this
' runtime reports 21 — so it must be able to HOST jdtls, an Eclipse/OSGi
' application. java.compiler, java.instrument, jdk.attach, jdk.jdi, jdk.zipfs and
' jdk.compiler are there for jdtls, and they cost 13 MB.
'
' ── THE THREE APT PACKAGES THAT ONLY LOOK COSMETIC ──────────────────────────
' fontconfig, fonts-dejavu-core and libharfbuzz0b are installed explicitly
' because they are what openjdk-21-jre-headless used to pull in for free.
' Debian's libfontmanager.so links against the SYSTEM harfbuzz; a jlink runtime
' carries the .so but not the dependency, so PlantUML died in SunFontManager's
' static initialiser — before drawing anything, and only at first render. Found
' by building it, not by reading.
'
' That is also why the layer that writes the plantuml shim RENDERS one diagram:
'
'   printf '@startuml\nAlice -> Bob: floor\n@enduml\n' > /tmp/floor.puml
'   plantuml -tpng -o /tmp /tmp/floor.puml && test -s /tmp/floor.png
'
' A missing module then fails the BUILD, rather than a sandbox an operator is
' already sitting in.
'
' ── WHY JAVA_HOME IS SET WHERE IT IS ────────────────────────────────────────
' `ENV JAVA_HOME=/opt/jre PATH="/opt/jre/bin:${PATH}"` sits immediately after the
' `COPY --from=jre-builder`, not in the ENV block at the end of the file, because
' the RUN that follows asserts the runtime works and an ENV declared later is not
' in scope for it. `java` on PATH is also exactly what `_install_jdtls` probes.
'
' ── COPY --chmod, NOT COPY-THEN-chmod ───────────────────────────────────────
' The COPYs carry `--chmod=0755` so the mode arrives with the file. Setting it in
' a later RUN copied each binary UP into that layer in full — overlayfs has no
' other way to record a metadata change — storing proveo-entrypoint and
' plantuml-lsp twice. Two of the three chmods were no-ops anyway, because
' `go build` already writes 0755.
'
' ── proveo/base-node: ONE NODE, ONE pnpm, ONE BUN ───────────────────────────
' NODE_MAJOR=22 via nodesource, pnpm@10.33.0, `unzip`.
'
' unzip is Bun's one documented prerequisite on Linux, and it lands here so every
' Node consumer inherits it (opencode used to install its own copy).
'
' `rm -rf /usr/include/node` is in the SAME RUN as the nodesource install:
' nodesource's deb ships 65 MB of C++ headers for building native addons, and
' node-gyp fetches its own into ~/.cache/node-gyp anyway — only an explicit
' `--nodedir` reads these. A later RUN would delete the path and keep the bytes.
'
' BUN IS PINNED TWICE — by version AND by the digest published in that release's
' SHASUMS256.txt:
'   ARG BUN_VERSION=1.4.0
'   ARG BUN_SHA256_X64=2d03fb5fb83ac8b567aca0a281b2ce1a1a19d488f56c2968d88c3f25e92fe452
'   ARG BUN_SHA256_AARCH64=4b1a332ee861983eb93bcfe6f770fff94e3e31b2c388bdaea3c8ed35e58eed0e
' From the GitHub release zip. NOT `npm install -g bun`: its postinstall fetches
' the same binary through the registry, unverified by anything the Dockerfile
' names. NOT the install script: unpinned by default, and it writes to ~/.bun.
' The x64 asset is the AVX2 build — Bun's `-baseline` variant exists for
' pre-Haswell CPUs and is not what this fleet runs on. `bunx` is a symlink to
' `bun`, as the installer makes it. `test "$(bun --version)" = "${BUN_VERSION}"`
' makes the pin a fact about the image.
'
' Which pins the SEED honours, and why bun rides this layer rather than a
' harness, is _spec/_runtimes/toolchain-provisioning.puml.
'
' ── proveo/base-node-lsp: SIX SERVERS, AND A PRUNE IN THE SAME RUN ──────────
' `npm install -g --no-optional`: typescript-language-server,
' vscode-langservers-extracted, bash-language-server,
' dockerfile-language-server-nodejs, yaml-language-server, pyright.
'
' Measured in the installed tree: 11 MB of `*.map` and 18 MB of changelogs,
' readmes and docs/ directories. Source maps only ever improve a stack trace from
' a server nobody debugs from inside a sandbox.
'
' `test/` directories are deliberately NOT pruned — some packages load fixtures
' from them at runtime, and 29 MB is not worth finding out which.
'
' ── proveo/base's FLOOR PROBE ───────────────────────────────────────────────
' defs/base/ensure.sh checks git + gh + jq + an executable
' /usr/local/bin/proveo-entrypoint. No browser, no Node, no Python: those moved
' out of the base, and the probe states the contract rather than restating the
' package list.
'
' ── BUILD CONTEXT DIFFERS BY LAYER, AND IT IS NOT AN OVERSIGHT ──────────────
' defs/base/build.sh passes REPO_ROOT, because the entrypoint builder copies
' cmd/ and internal/ from the module. defs/base-node/build.sh and
' defs/base-node-lsp/build.sh pass SCRIPT_DIR: those Dockerfiles COPY nothing
' from the repo, so the narrower context is free.

node "Builder stages — discarded after the copy" as B <<host>> {
  component "proveo-entrypoint-builder\n""golang:1.26-trixie""" as GO <<app>>
  component "jre-builder\n""debian:trixie-slim"" + jdk + binutils" as JRE <<app>>
}

node "proveo/base — the universal floor" as BASE <<host>> {
  component """/usr/local/bin/proveo-entrypoint""\n""/usr/local/bin/plantuml-lsp""" as BIN <<app>>
  database "``/opt/jre`` — jlink, 72 MB\n20 modules, zip-6, stripped" as JLINK <<db>>
  component "``/opt/plantuml.jar`` + shim\nrendered once, at build" as PUML <<app>>
  component "git · gh · jq · tmux · ripgrep\ngraphviz · fontconfig · harfbuzz" as APT <<app>>
}

node "proveo/base-node" as BN <<host>> {
  component "node 22 · pnpm 10.33.0 · unzip" as NODE <<app>>
  component "bun 1.4.0 + bunx\nversion AND sha256 pinned" as BUN <<app>>
}

node "proveo/base-node-lsp" as BNL <<host>> {
  component "six language servers\n""npm install -g --no-optional""" as LSP <<app>>
}

component "``COPY . .`` into the Go builder\n201 MB node_modules · a README busts it" as WIDE <<error>>
component "``default-jre-headless`` 194 MB\nfor one jar, on all 14 images" as FATJRE <<error>>
component "SunFontManager static initialiser\nno system harfbuzz — dies before drawing" as FONT <<error>>
component "a delete in a LATER RUN\nremoves the path, keeps the bytes" as LATER <<error>>
component "``npm install -g bun``\npostinstall fetches, nothing verifies" as NPMBUN <<error>>

GO ARROW_MAIN BIN : ""COPY --chmod=0755 --from=…""
JRE ARROW_MAIN JLINK : ""COPY --from=jre-builder /opt/jre""
GO ARROW_ERROR WIDE : avoided — ""COPY cmd"" + ""COPY internal""
FATJRE ARROW_MAIN JRE : replaced by ""jlink"", 194 → 72 MB
JLINK ARROW_MAIN PUML : the shim execs this runtime
APT ARROW_ERROR FONT : prevented — harfbuzz, fontconfig\nand dejavu are explicit now
PUML ARROW_MAIN PUML : renders ""/tmp/floor.puml"" at BUILD
BASE ARROW_MAIN BN
BN ARROW_MAIN BNL
NODE ARROW_ERROR LATER : ""rm -rf /usr/include/node""\nshares the nodesource RUN
LSP ARROW_ERROR LATER : the ""*.map"" and docs prune\nshares the install RUN
BUN ARROW_ERROR NPMBUN : never — release zip,\nversion + SHASUMS256 digest

note bottom of GO
  **Upstream code goes above the source copy.**
  plantuml-lsp owes nothing to this repo, so
  installing it below ""COPY"" made every edit in
  the tree re-run the fetch. Above it, the layer
  is cached until the version moves.
end note

note bottom of WIDE
  **The context is the whole repo.**
  Every def builds from the root, so ""COPY . .""
  baked 201 MB of node_modules into a builder and
  invalidated the compile on any file — a README
  edit re-ran ""go build"".
end note

note right of JLINK
  **The module list is deliberately not minimal.**
  A plantuml-only prune is 59 MB and breaks jdtls:
  ""_install_jdtls"" uses the floor's java once
  ""_java_major"" reports 21, so this runtime must
  HOST an OSGi app. Six modules for it, 13 MB.
end note

note bottom of JRE
  **binutils is a build dep, not a runtime one.**
  ""jlink --strip-debug"" runs ""objcopy"" on
  Debian's OpenJDK and fails with 'Cannot run
  program objcopy' without it. It stays in the
  builder stage, which ships nothing.
end note

note bottom of FONT
  **A jlink runtime has the .so, not its deps.**
  libfontmanager links the SYSTEM harfbuzz, so
  PlantUML died in a static initialiser at FIRST
  render — nothing earlier. Found by building it,
  now caught by rendering a diagram at build.
end note

note right of PUML
  **The build renders a diagram on purpose.**
  A missing module is otherwise invisible until an
  operator asks for a picture inside a sandbox, so
  the layer that writes the shim proves it works
  before the image is allowed to exist.
end note

note bottom of BUN
  **Two pins, because one is a request.**
  The version names the release; the SHASUMS256
  digest names the bytes. The x64 asset is the
  AVX2 build — the ""-baseline"" variant is for
  pre-Haswell CPUs this fleet does not run on.
end note

note bottom of LATER
  **A deletion only saves bytes in the RUN that
  created them.** overlayfs records a later ""rm""
  as a whitedout path over a layer that still
  carries the content, so the image is no smaller
  and the reader believes it is.
end note

note bottom of LSP
  **""test/"" is kept, and that is a judgement.**
  Maps and docs are 29 MB and safe to drop; some
  packages load fixtures from ""test/"" at runtime
  and another 29 MB is not worth discovering
  which one does it in a sandbox.
end note

note bottom of BIN
  **The mode travels with the COPY.**
  A later ""chmod"" copies each binary up into
  layer in full, storing both twice, and two of
  the three were no-ops because ""go build""
  already writes 0755.
end note

@enduml
